WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.250
18 July 2017.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.110
Coverack, a coastal village on the east
side of Cornwall's Lizard peninsula.

3
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.610
A thunderstorm hits, with hail
as large as fifty pence pieces.

4
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.610
In three hours, between 165 and
201 millimetres of rain fall:

5
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.130
three times July's monthly average.

6
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.270
The upper figure broke
the UK three-hour record,

7
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.090
according to Met Office records.

8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.830
44 properties in Coverack flooded inside.

9
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.170
One family was rescued
by coastguard helicopter.

10
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.350
So why did this village flood so fast?

11
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.730
In this mission, you'll
take a UK flash flood apart,

12
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.090
cause by cause, and
trace its consequences.

13
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:48.370
Then you'll weigh how to protect a village
where no flood scheme was found practicable.

14
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.770
Your mission: explain why the
flood hit Coverack so fast.
